<tr valign="top" height="300" >
<td tEditID="c1r2" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r2" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal"></p><p class="MsoHeader"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Dear
<span style="background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">[BPL Name]</span>,<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoHeader"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">**Add
personal introduction**</span><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Arial"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Thank
you so much for your support and commitment to increasing our diverse donor
base.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Did
you know that your current drive is collecting <span style="background:yellow;
mso-highlight:yellow">XX%</span> of diverse collections? Through additional
education and focused recruitment, we can work to increase our diversity
collections together.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Diverse
blood donors play a critical role in helping patients in emergencies or
battling diseases like sickle cell to receive the most compatible blood match.
It is essential that donor diversity match patient diversity, so we must work
to increase the number of blood donors from all ethnic and racial groups.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Answer
the call to help save those in need by hosting a Red Cross blood drive to help
support patients and families.<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Why
does </span><a href="https://www.redcrossblood.org/donate-blood/blood-types/diversity.html"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">donor diversity</span></a><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> matter?</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul style="margin-top:0in" type="disc">
 <li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst" style="margin-left:0in;mso-add-space:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The
     best blood type match for patients with rare blood types often comes from
     donors of the same race or similar ethnicity. Certain blood types are
     unique to specific racial and ethnic groups.</span><o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:0in;mso-add-space:
     auto;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:
     &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">If a patient receives a transfusion that is not a
     close match, they may form antibodies. Individuals who receive frequent
     blood transfusions, such as patients with sickle cell disease, need to
     receive the most compatible match possible to avoid developing
     complications.</span><o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="margin-left:0in;mso-add-space:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Diverse
     populations also play a critical role in meeting the constant need for
     blood because type O blood is most often in critical supply and most often
     needed by hospitals. 51% of people who are Black or African American and
     57% of people who are Hispanic or Latino are type O.</span><o:p></o:p></li>
</ul><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">As
a leader in your community, you can make a significant impact by hosting <span style="background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">a/another</span> Red Cross blood
drive.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
color:red">[Add if January/February]</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Encourage
donors to give blood in honor of Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. and in celebration
of Black History Month. It’s important to emphasis how diverse communities can
help support sickle cell patients through blood donation. Many schools,
churches, and organizations are already involved in activities and community
projects during this time, and incorporating a blood drive is another great way
to bring the community together in the spirit of compassion, diversity and
unity.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Please
consider hosting a Red Cross blood drive this January or February to help bring
awareness to the need for diverse donors.<o:p></o:p></span></i></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
color:red">[Add if March]</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Encourage
donors to give blood this month in honor of César Chávez Day, celebrated on
March 31. It’s a perfect time to come together as a community in honor of the
civil rights and labor movement activist and his championship of helping those
in need. Donations from those in the Latino community are especially important
in the treatment of trauma patients and others needing emergency blood
transfusions because more than half of all Hispanics/Latinos in the U.S. have
type O blood. Help fight for those who are suffering by coming together as a
community to ensure blood is available for those who need it.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Please
consider hosting a Red Cross blood drive this March to help bring awareness to
the need for diverse donors.<o:p></o:p></span></i></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
color:red">[Add if June/July]</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">We
need you this summer, as donations tend to drop, to host <span style="background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">a/another</span> Red Cross blood
drive. June is a special time of recognition, with </span><a href="https://vimeo.com/696167273/ac3155272a"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Dr. Charles R. Drew’s birthday</span></a><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> on June 3 and World
Sickle Cell Awareness Day and Juneteenth on June 19. It’s the perfect time to
highlight communities coming together – and what better way to celebrate
community than by hosting a blood drive and saving lives? Blood donations from
diverse individuals are crucial for meeting the transfusion needs of patients,
especially those with sickle cell disease.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Please
consider hosting a Red Cross blood drive this June to help bring awareness to
the need for diverse donors.<o:p></o:p></span></i></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
color:red">[Add if August/September/October]</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">September
is </span><a href="https://www.redcrossblood.org/donate-blood/blood-types/diversity/african-american-blood-donors.html"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">National Sickle Cell
Awareness Month</span></a><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">
and an ideal time to highlight the unique blood needs of individuals living
with this genetic disease. Patients with sickle cell disease may rely on
regular blood transfusions throughout their lives to prevent sickle cell
complications such as organ and tissue damage, severe pain, and strokes. One in
3 African American blood donors are a match for people with sickle cell disease
– diverse communities can help support these patients through blood donation.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In
addition, National Hispanic Heritage Month is observed Sept. 15-Oct. 15 to
celebrate unity and appreciation of the diverse contributions and cultural
heritage of Hispanic and Latino Americans.</span> <span style="font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Donations from those in the Latino community
are especially important in the treatment of trauma patients and others needing
emergency blood transfusions because more than half of all Hispanics/Latinos in
the U.S. have type O blood. This is a perfect time to come together as a
community by organizing a blood drive to help patients battling blood disorders
like sickle cell disease, as well as those needing an organ transplant,
suffering from a traumatic injury or a new mom experiencing a complicated
childbirth.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><i><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Please
consider hosting a Red Cross blood drive this September or October to help
bring awareness to the need for diverse donors.<o:p></o:p></span></i></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Let’s
get your drive scheduled and help provide hope to patients in need!<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Best regards,</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoHeader"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">[Your Name]</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoHeader"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">[Your Title]</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoHeader">























































































</p><p class="MsoHeader"><span style="font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">[Your Email]</span><o:p></o:p></p><p></p>]]></td>
</tr>
